{"entries":[{"caption":"Conditional relationships between nightly mean relative humidity and bat activity for (a) low-, (b) mid-, and (c) high-frequency echolocation groups. Lines show posterior median expected numbers of 5-min detection intervals per night, with inner and outer ribbons representing 50% and 89% credible intervals, respectively. Predictions were generated from the frequency-group-specific Bayesian generalized additive models while holding the other environmental predictors at their reference values and averaging over the seasonal effect. Note that y-axis scales differ among panels to emphasize the shape and uncertainty of the response within each frequency group.","key":"fig-humidity","order":{"number":3,"section":[1,4,2,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Seasonal variation in community-level bat acoustic activity across eight sites in the northern Sierra Nevada, California, April–October 2015. (a) Total seasonal pattern from the day-of-year model, shown as the posterior distribution of the equal-site averaged expected number of 5-min intervals per night in which a bat call occurred. (b) Conditional seasonal pattern from the environmental model after accounting for nightly mean temperature, relative humidity, and lunar phase; the curve is likewise averaged equally across sites. (c) Site-specific seasonal phenology from the total seasonal model. Thin gray lines show posterior median trajectories for individual sites; the black line and shaded bands show the equal-site averaged seasonal trajectory. In panels a and b, and for the average in panel c, lines indicate posterior medians and shaded bands indicate 50%, 80%, and 89% credible intervals from darkest to lightest.","key":"fig-seasonality","order":{"number":1,"section":[1,3,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Conditional relationships between lunar illumination and bat activity for (a) low-, (b) mid-, and (c) high-frequency groups. Lunar illumination ranges from 0 (new moon) to 1 (full moon). Lines show posterior median expected numbers of 5-min detection intervals per night, with inner and outer ribbons representing 50% and 89% credible intervals, respectively. Predictions were generated from the frequency-group-specific Bayesian generalized additive models while holding temperature and relative humidity at their reference values and averaging over the seasonal effect. Note that y-axis scales differ among panels to emphasize the shape and uncertainty of the response within each frequency group.","key":"fig-lunar","order":{"number":4,"section":[1,4,4,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Conditional relationships between nightly mean temperature and bat acoustic activity for (a) low-frequency, (b) mid-frequency, and (c) high-frequency echolocation groups at eight sites in the northern Sierra Nevada, California. Predictions were generated across the observed temperature range and averaged over the observed distribution of sampled days of year, with each site weighted equally; relative humidity and lunar phase were held at their reference values. Lines show posterior medians and shaded ribbons show 50%, 80%, and 89% credible intervals (darkest to lightest). Y-axis scales differ among panels to emphasize differences in response shape among frequency groups.","key":"fig-temperature","order":{"number":2,"section":[1,4,1,0,0,0,0]}}],"headings":["results","sampling-and-acoustic-activity","model-development-and-adequacy","seasonal-activity","echolocation-frequency-groups","temperature-responses-among-frequency-groups","frequency-dependent-humidity-responses","frequency-specific-seasonal-phenology","lunar-responses-among-frequency-groups","summary-of-principal-findings","tables-and-figures-to-generate"]}